Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:05.70,Default,,0,0,0,,In my mother's village, there is one big\Ntree where news arrives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.40,0:00:13.32,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother never went to school. She\Ncannot read a single word.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.40,0:00:19.08,Default,,0,0,0,,But every letter I send, she holds like\Nit is gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.40,0:00:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,So she walks to the tree and waits for\NSelam, the neighbour's daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.40,0:00:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Selam reads my words out loud, slowly,\Ntwice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.40,0:00:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother listens with her eyes closed,\Nas if I am the one speaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.40,0:00:49.90,Default,,0,0,0,,She keeps every letter in this box.\NTwelve years of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.40,0:00:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,But she could never write back. My\Nletters only travelled one way.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.40,0:01:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,This year, I came home with something\Nnew.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.40,0:01:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I showed her one button. Press, speak,\Nlet go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.40,0:01:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, every morning, I hear her voice:\N"My child, I am well. And you?"
